WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.046
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for vowel teams and the bossy r.

2
00:00:04.496 --> 00:00:09.868
It starts where Cap to Cape ends. Here is a word with a team of two letters that make one sound.

3
00:00:13.404 --> 00:00:14.452
The word is star.

4
00:00:15.352 --> 00:00:23.661
The goal of this plan is a child who finds the team first, and reads words like play, star, bird and cloud that were never seen before.

5
00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:29.949
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

6
00:00:30.749 --> 00:00:35.354
This plan is for a child who reads words like cake, feet, rain and boat.

7
00:00:35.804 --> 00:00:39.917
Often the child reads each letter on its own, and the word comes out wrong.

8
00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:43.590
Or stops at words like play, star, bird and cloud.

9
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.111
It is a normal step. In these words two letters work as a team and make one sound.

10
00:00:49.561 --> 00:00:54.075
Some teams are a new way to write a sound your child knows. Some are new sounds.

11
00:00:54.525 --> 00:00:59.029
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

12
00:00:59.429 --> 00:01:04.574
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

13
00:01:05.024 --> 00:01:10.281
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

14
00:01:10.881 --> 00:01:16.606
Days two, three and four teach new spellings of long sounds your child knows from Cap to Cape.

15
00:01:17.056 --> 00:01:21.174
Day five is a halfway check. It tells you to go on, or to go back.

16
00:01:21.624 --> 00:01:27.012
Days six and seven teach the bossy r. It changes the sound of the vowel in front of it.

17
00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:32.126
Then two new sounds, as in coin and in cloud, and on day nine a story.

18
00:01:32.576 --> 00:01:37.409
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

19
00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:42.354
When a word goes wrong, do not say the word. Say the same words, every time.

20
00:01:42.804 --> 00:01:45.708
Find the team. What sound does it make? Then wait.

21
00:01:46.608 --> 00:01:53.095
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

22
00:01:53.545 --> 00:01:59.458
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps, with the words to say.

23
00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:03.056
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

24
00:02:03.506 --> 00:02:07.824
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three things to you at the end.

25
00:02:08.274 --> 00:02:13.147
On six of the days your child has a track to listen to. You press play and step away.

26
00:02:13.947 --> 00:02:19.074
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, and scissors for the cards on day two.

27
00:02:19.524 --> 00:02:24.612
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
